      "title": "Send a formal written complaint to BrightHome Appliances",
      "detail": "Since you have only spoken to the store manager verbally, send a formal written notice or email to BrightHome Appliances requesting a replacement. Under consumer law, a fault or shortcoming in the quality of goods is considered a defect [SRC:CPA2019-S2-10]. Refusing to take back defective goods and refund or resolve the issue within the period stated on the receipt or within 30 days is an unfair trade practice [SRC:CPA2019-S2-47-viii]."
    },
    {
      "title": "Register a grievance with the National Consumer Helpline",
      "detail": "If BrightHome Appliances does not provide a resolution, report your dispute to the National Consumer Helpline. You can call their toll-free number 1915 (8 AM to 8 PM) or send a message on WhatsApp to +918800001915 [SRC:NCH-CONTACT]. You can also file a grievance on consumerhelpline.gov.in [SRC:NCH-CONTACT]."
    },
    {
      "title": "Consider filing a complaint with the District Consumer Commission",
      "detail": "If the matter remains unresolved, you may file a formal complaint with the District Consumer Commission [SRC:CPA2019-S35-1]. The District Commission handles cases where the amount paid is up to Rs. 50 lakh [SRC:JUR2021-R3]. For your claim of Rs. 32,000, the official filing fee is Nil [SRC:CDRC2023-R7-FEE]. Complaints can be submitted online through e-jagriti.gov.in [SRC:CPA2019-S35-1], generally within two years from when the issue arose [SRC:CPA2019-S69]. The Commission may order remedies such as replacement or a refund [SRC:CPA2019-S39-1]."
    }
  ]
